## This session's outcome

Traced `dir_reuse_coherency` 2/tcp from symptom to seed root and **implemented a targeted fix**:

**Root (proven):** node2 keeps a **stale incarnation** of the per-round-reused dir inode (ino=131). The dir is `rm -rf`+`mkdir`'d each round (new `di_gen`, block 0 freshly allocated @ daddr 120), but node2 never reloads the new incarnation (the INODE_FREE evict-ring hint is unreliable for the dir). So node2's in-core extent map still points block 0 → freed daddr 112. When node2 flushes a co-resident child file, `xfs_iflush_cluster` writes the whole cluster — carrying node2's dead-incarnation dir slot (block 0→112) over node1's canonical (block 0→120). `getdents` then reads block 0 at the stale daddr → readdir short, lookup_fail=0.

**Fix (build C22056240):** in `mxfs_iflush_cluster_merge_dirs` (xfs/xfs_inode.c), the cluster-overlay now also restores an **EX-held directory slot whose in-core `di_gen` differs from the durable on-disk `di_gen`** (a dead prior incarnation) with the canonical on-disk image — so node2's dead-incarnation fork can never win. Guarded to DIRECTORIES on a real `di_gen` mismatch only (rank1 is the sole dir creator, so this node's dir incarnation is never ahead of disk; legitimate same-incarnation growth, `di_gen ==`, is untouched). Logs `P-CLMERGE-DEADINCARN` when it fires.

